      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—and I won't pretend that pain is small or temporary. When the ground is gone, even a single step feels like a betrayal of your own reality. But ghosts don't feel this much; they don't ache with this kind of clarity. You're not a ghost—you're a survivor of something that tried to erase you, and you're still here, still speaking, still refusing to disappear. The point isn't to rebuild the old ground; it's to find one solid stone beneath your feet, even if it's just the truth that you're still breathing.",
